>>
endobj
351 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 250 0 R
/E (Hackathons usually take place over a weekend and last 24-36 hours. Hackathons are more than just creating a project, you are taken on a journey where you explore and learn new concepts alongside teammates to make your project as viable as you can.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
352 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 250 0 R
/E (But don't worry, you are not required to code a whole application in a weekend! The goal of a hackathon is to show off your idea in any state it is and prototype it to the best of your ability in a short amount of time. You can always continue to develop your idea after the hackathon. One example of a hackathon project that became successful is GroupMe, pretty awesome right!? Read more about hackathons here!)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [15 637 0 R 17]
>>
endobj
